<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - March statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - March statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production in May and consumption, imports and exports of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in January/May compared with 1995 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>  METAL		PRODUCTION (MAY)    CONSUMPTION (JAN/MAY)</p>
<p>		    1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  100,900     99,900	 197,399    251,191</p>
<p> Lead			 0	1,169	     n/a     29,039</p>
<p> Copper		15,246     12,371	  80,437     88,915</p>
<p> Tin		    1,433	1,295	   2,842	1,679</p>
<p> Magnesium		 81	   17	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,344	1,250	   7,116	7,723</p>
<p> Zinc		  14,923     14,625	  50,531     83,593</p>
<p> METAL		 EXPORTS (JAN/MAY)	  IMPORTS (JAN/MAY)</p>
<p>		 1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  347,277    292,419	  38,987     48,886</p>
<p> Lead		   1,507	   48	   8,966     22,780</p>
<p> Copper		35,436     17,236	 255,127     79,738</p>
<p> Tin		    4,546	3,892		11	  105</p>
<p> Magnesium	    1,088	   63	     711	1,186</p>
<p> Nickel		 2,489	1,971	   3,205	2,816</p>
<p> Zinc		  26,769     13,300	   3,201     23,119</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
